<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:144%;">Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is predicted by a neural network without a rigorous mathematical explicit expression. It may be unable to be exactly equal to the original required <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for various reasons, including the performance of the neural network and the noise. This error could accumulate when finding the solution to the ODE by iterative methods. Therefore, understanding the bounds of this error is crucial for assessing and improving the denoising algorithm of flow matching. In this section, we will prove that this error has an upper bound as</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widetilde{Z}_{t_{0}}-Z_{t_{0}}|\leq e^{\Lambda}|\delta_{0}|+\frac{e^{\Lambda}-1}{\Lambda}\max_{1\leq i\leq N}|\delta_{i}|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widetilde{Z}_{t_{0}}-Z_{t_{0}}|\leq e^{\Lambda}|\delta_{0}|+\frac{e^{\Lambda}-1}{\Lambda}\max_{1\leq i\leq N}|\delta_{i}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the ODE solution with perturbation, <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the ODE solution by iterative method without any perturbation ideally, <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}(i=0,1,2,\dots,N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}(i=0,1,2,\dots,N)</annotation></semantics></math> is the perturbation at step <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda=(41/24)L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=(41/24)L</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz constant).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> The process of solving ODE is determining <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the given <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be achieved using the general Runge-Kutta method, which takes the form:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t_{i-1}}=Z_{t_{i}}+h\Phi_{i}(Z_{t_{i}})~(i=1,2,3,\dots,N)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t_{i-1}}=Z_{t_{i}}+h\Phi_{i}(Z_{t_{i}})~(i=1,2,3,\dots,N),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is the hyperparameter associated with the time step configuration, and <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{i}(Z_{t_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{i}(Z_{t_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the incremental function of the Runge-Kutta method at step <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the time step in RF is uniform (<math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t_{i}=\Delta t_{j}~\text{for}~i\neq j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t_{i}=\Delta t_{j}~\text{for}~i\neq j)</annotation></semantics></math>), it can be simplified that <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\Delta t_{i}(i=0,1,2,\dots,N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\Delta t_{i}(i=0,1,2,\dots,N)</annotation></semantics></math>. And the <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{i}(Z_{t_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{i}(Z_{t_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{i}(Z_{t_{i}})=\sum_{j=1}^{r}b_{j}K_{j}^{i}(Z_{t_{i}}),~\text{where}~K_{s}^{i}(Z_{t_{i}})=v_{\theta}\left(Z_{t_{i}}-\Delta{t_{i}}\sum_{j=1}^{s-1}{a_{sj}K_{j}^{i}},t_{i}-c_{s}\Delta t_{i},\mathcal{P}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{i}(Z_{t_{i}})=\sum_{j=1}^{r}b_{j}K_{j}^{i}(Z_{t_{i}}),~\text{where}~K_{s}^{i}(Z_{t_{i}})=v_{\theta}\left(Z_{t_{i}}-\Delta{t_{i}}\sum_{j=1}^{s-1}{a_{sj}K_{j}^{i}},t_{i}-c_{s}\Delta t_{i},\mathcal{P}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">In conjunction with Equation (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Runge-Kutta Approximation and Decoupled Attention for Rectified Flow Inversion and Semantic Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), the perturbed process can be represented as:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i-1}}=\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i}}+h\left[\Phi_{i}(\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i}})+\delta_{i}\right]~(i=1,2,3,\dots,N),~\widetilde{Z}_{t_{N}}=Z_{t_{N}}+\delta_{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i-1}}=\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i}}+h\left[\Phi_{i}(\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i}})+\delta_{i}\right]~(i=1,2,3,\dots,N),~\widetilde{Z}_{t_{N}}=Z_{t_{N}}+\delta_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">According to Runge <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, it is shown that for the 4-th order RF solver in this work:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Phi_{i}(y)-\Phi_{i}(x)|\leq\left[1+\frac{Lh}{2!}+\frac{(Lh)^{2}}{3!}+\frac{(Lh)^{4}}{4!}\right]L|y-x|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Phi_{i}(y)-\Phi_{i}(x)|\leq\left[1+\frac{Lh}{2!}+\frac{(Lh)^{2}}{3!}+\frac{(Lh)^{4}}{4!}\right]L|y-x|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> can be any Lipschitz constant of <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. And from Equation (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Runge-Kutta Approximation and Decoupled Attention for Rectified Flow Inversion and Semantic Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), it can be obtained that</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Phi_{i}(y)-\Phi_{i}(x)|\leq\Lambda|y-x|,~\text{for}~0&lt;h\leq h_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Phi_{i}(y)-\Phi_{i}(x)|\leq\Lambda|y-x|,~\text{for}~0&lt;h\leq h_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Take the <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}=1/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}=1/L</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be obtained that <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda=(41/24)L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=(41/24)L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By substracting the ralations in Equation (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Runge-Kutta Approximation and Decoupled Attention for Rectified Flow Inversion and Semantic Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) from the corresponding ones in Equation (<a href="#A1.E18" title="In Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Runge-Kutta Approximation and Decoupled Attention for Rectified Flow Inversion and Semantic Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) and by using the Equation (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Runge-Kutta Approximation and Decoupled Attention for Rectified Flow Inversion and Semantic Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), it can be obtained that</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i-1}}-Z_{t_{i-1}}|\leq(1+h\Lambda)|\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i}}-Z_{t_{i}}|+h|\delta_{i-1}|~(i=1,2,3,\dots,N)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i-1}}-Z_{t_{i-1}}|\leq(1+h\Lambda)|\widetilde{Z}_{t_{i}}-Z_{t_{i}}|+h|\delta_{i-1}|~(i=1,2,3,\dots,N).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+h\Lambda)^{n}\leq e^{nh\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+h\Lambda)^{n}\leq e^{nh\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be iteratively obtained:</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widetilde{Z}_{t_{0}}-Z_{t_{0}}|\leq e^{\Lambda T}|\delta_{0}|+\frac{e^{\Lambda T}-1}{\Lambda}\max_{1\leq i\leq N}|\delta_{i}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widetilde{Z}_{t_{0}}-Z_{t_{0}}|\leq e^{\Lambda T}|\delta_{0}|+\frac{e^{\Lambda T}-1}{\Lambda}\max_{1\leq i\leq N}|\delta_{i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide additional experimental results to further demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed method.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Additional Implementation Details</h3>

<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Visualization of Word-Pixel Response Maps for MM-DiT Architectures</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Input caption with <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> words <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{w_{1},\dots,w_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{w_{1},\dots,w_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, Target word index <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Word-pixel response maps <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\{R_{g}|g\in G\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\{R_{g}|g\in G\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t_{N}}\leftarrow\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t_{N}}\leftarrow\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="algorithm1.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sample initial latent </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\text{T5}(\mathcal{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>T5</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\text{T5}(\mathcal{C})</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">compute prompt embedding </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\rm{cache}}\leftarrow\text{None}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>cache</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext>None</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\rm{cache}}\leftarrow\text{None}</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="algorithm1.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">initialize cached decoupled attention maps </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leftarrow[\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leftarrow[\,]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.7.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.4.7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t_{i-1}}\leftarrow z_{t_{i}}+(t_{i-1}-t_{i})\cdot v_{\theta}^{\rm{cache}}(z_{t_{i}},t_{i},\mathcal{P},A_{\rm{cache}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>cache</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>cache</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t_{i-1}}\leftarrow z_{t_{i}}+(t_{i-1}-t_{i})\cdot v_{\theta}^{\rm{cache}}(z_{t_{i}},t_{i},\mathcal{P},A_{\rm{cache}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\rm{cache}}\leftarrow A_{\rm{cache}}/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>cache</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>cache</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\rm{cache}}\leftarrow A_{\rm{cache}}/N</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.10.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{g}\leftarrow A_{\rm{cache}}[:,g]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>cache</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{g}\leftarrow A_{\rm{cache}}[:,g]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.4.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">extract target attention maps </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{g}\leftarrow{\rm{resize}}(A_{g},H\times W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>resize</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{g}\leftarrow{\rm{resize}}(A_{g},H\times W)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">resize to image resolution </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R{\rm{.append}}(A_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>append</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R{\rm{.append}}(A_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
