<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Ablation on Butcher Tableau.</span>
The Runge-Kutta method comprises a family of numerical solvers, each defined by a specific Butcher tableau. We report the results obtained using various Butcher tableaux, ranging from second-order to fourth-order solvers. For the second-order methods, we include the midpoint, Heun’s, and Ralston’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> methods, which are given by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{B}_{\text{midpoint}}^{(2)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|cc}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;0&amp;1\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{Heun}}^{(2)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|cc}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
1&amp;1&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{Ralston}}^{(2)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|cc}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{2}{3}&amp;\frac{2}{3}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;\frac{3}{4}\end{array}\,\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>midpoint</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>Heun</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>Ralston</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.507em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{B}_{\text{midpoint}}^{(2)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|cc}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;0&amp;1\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{Heun}}^{(2)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|cc}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
1&amp;1&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{Ralston}}^{(2)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|cc}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{2}{3}&amp;\frac{2}{3}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;\frac{3}{4}\end{array}\,\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For the third-order methods, we include the Kutta’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, Heun’s, Ralston’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, Van der Houwen’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, and Strong Stability Preserving Runge-Kutta (SSPRK3) methods, each defined as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{B}_{\text{Kutta}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;0&amp;0\\
1&amp;-1&amp;2&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{6}&amp;\frac{2}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{6}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{Heun}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{3}&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{2}{3}&amp;0&amp;\frac{2}{3}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;0&amp;\frac{3}{4}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{Ralston}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{3}{4}&amp;0&amp;\frac{3}{4}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{2}{9}&amp;\frac{1}{3}&amp;\frac{4}{9}\end{array},\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>Kutta</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>Heun</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>Ralston</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{B}_{\text{Kutta}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;0&amp;0\\
1&amp;-1&amp;2&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{6}&amp;\frac{2}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{6}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{Heun}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{3}&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{2}{3}&amp;0&amp;\frac{2}{3}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;0&amp;\frac{3}{4}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{Ralston}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{3}{4}&amp;0&amp;\frac{3}{4}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{2}{9}&amp;\frac{1}{3}&amp;\frac{4}{9}\end{array},\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{B}_{\text{Houwen}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{8}{15}&amp;\frac{8}{15}&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{2}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;\frac{5}{12}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;0&amp;\frac{3}{4}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{SSPRK3}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
1&amp;1&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{6}&amp;\frac{1}{6}&amp;\frac{2}{3}\end{array}\,\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>Houwen</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>SSPRK3</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.507em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{B}_{\text{Houwen}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{8}{15}&amp;\frac{8}{15}&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{2}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;\frac{5}{12}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;0&amp;\frac{3}{4}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{SSPRK3}}^{(3)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
1&amp;1&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;\frac{1}{4}&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{6}&amp;\frac{1}{6}&amp;\frac{2}{3}\end{array}\,\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For the fourth-order methods, we include the classic, 3/8-rule, and Ralston’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> methods, which are defined by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{B}_{\text{classic}}^{(4)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|cccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{2}&amp;0&amp;\frac{1}{2}&amp;0&amp;0\\
1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;1&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{6}&amp;\frac{1}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{6}\end{array},\quad\textbf{B}_{\text{3/8-rule}}^{(4)}=\,\begin{array}[]{c|cccc}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{1}{3}&amp;\frac{1}{3}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\frac{2}{3}&amp;-\frac{1}{3}&amp;1&amp;0&amp;0\\
1&amp;1&amp;-1&amp;1&amp;0\\
\hline\cr&amp;\frac{1}{8}&amp;\frac{3}{8}&amp;\frac{3}{8}&amp;\frac{1}{8}\end{array},\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>classic</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="3.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">B</mtext><mtext>3/8-rule</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspa